<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Abacus buys video group for 5.26 mln rand.</title>
<headline>Abacus buys video group for 5.26 mln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Abacus Technology Holdings Ltd said on Tuesday it had acquired the businesses of the National Home Video Group as going concerns for 5.26 million rand.</p>
<p>The deal, effective retrospectively to March 1, 1997, will be settled by the allotting and issuing of 1.1 million ordinary Abacus shares at 180 cents each and 1.82 million non-voting &quot;N&quot; shares at 180 cents.</p>
<p>Abacus said the net assets acquired, excluding intangibles, amounted to some 700,000 rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
